{% comment %}
  sections/main-faq.liquid

  One arrangement: a heading cluster over the questions.

  ## Nothing here is FAQ-specific that did not have to be

  The heading cluster is a static **Section header** block — the same file, the
  same settings, the same gradient — so there are no heading or text settings on
  this section to drift from it. The preset fills it with the block's own
  *Section header (vertical)* arrangement: a subheading pill, a gradient h2 and
  a paragraph, centred. Those values are copied rather than referenced because
  `content_for` names a block *type*, not one of that type's presets — there is
  no syntax for "insert this block the way its vertical preset would".

  ## A preset's blocks are an array, and a template's are a hash

  The two look interchangeable and are not, which is worth writing down because
  getting it wrong fails silently rather than loudly.

      preset (in this schema)     "blocks": [ { "type": …, "settings": … } ]
      template (templates/*.json) "blocks": { "<id>": { … } }, "block_order": […]

  A preset written in the template's hash form is not rejected — Shopify simply
  ignores it, and the merchant adds the section and gets an empty one. So the
  preset below is an array, and the heading cluster carries `"static": true`
  with the same `id` the `content_for` tag above names. Static ids never appear
  in a `block_order`, because a static block cannot be reordered.

  Padding is `snippets/spacing.liquid`, width is `snippets/container.liquid`,
  and the disclosure animation is `<accordion-element>` from
  `assets/modules.js`.

  What this file contributes is the arrangement, and the arrangement is a flex
  container over the section's own children. **Direction** turns it from a stack
  into a row, which is how the heading cluster ends up beside the questions —
  they are siblings, and nothing here goes looking for which child is which.

  That is the whole layout switch. A tab strip, a media column and a search field
  were all settings this section carried, and all three are gone: a store that
  wants questions beside a picture builds that from blocks rather than from a
  mode hidden behind a select.

  The layout controls are the Group block's, down to the setting ids — Alignment
  is always the horizontal axis, Position always the vertical, and `base.css`
  decides which CSS property reads which. A merchant who has laid out a Group
  already knows every control here.

  ## The old category block is gone

  `faq-category` packed a whole category into one rich text field, alternating
  question and answer by paragraph order, and a merchant who mis-ordered one
  paragraph got a silently wrong page they could not see the cause of. It is
  replaced by real blocks — an Accordion holding Accordion rows — because a row
  that is a block can carry an icon, an open-by-default state and its own
  padding, and none of that survives being encoded as paragraph order.

  ## The surface is the footer's, and deliberately so

  Background, border, corners, animation and padding are the same settings, the
  same ids and the same snippets `sections/footer.liquid` uses. Nothing here is
  a second implementation: the picture is `snippets/background-media.liquid`,
  the reveal is `snippets/motion-attrs.liquid` feeding `<motion-effect>`, and
  the padding is `snippets/spacing.liquid`. A merchant who has set up one of
  these panels already knows this one.
{% endcomment %}


{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings

  comment
    The background is the colour scheme's until the merchant says otherwise:
    either a colour of their own, or a picture behind the whole section.

    The colour is emitted as a real `background` declaration rather than a
    custom property because `color-scheme-container` paints a background *and*
    a gradient image, and only the shorthand clears both.
  endcomment
  assign background_media = s.background_media | default: 'none'
  assign has_background_media = false
  if background_media != 'none'
    assign has_background_media = true
  endif

  assign background_paint = ''
  if has_background_media == false
    assign background_paint = s.background_color | default: ''
  endif

  comment
    Opacity goes into the colour, not onto the element: `opacity` on the section
    would fade the questions along with the frame.

    With no colour picked the border is `currentColor`, which the colour filters
    cannot take an alpha channel from — there is no channel to read until the
    scheme resolves it in the browser. `color-mix` does the same fade at that
    point instead, so both paths honour the slider.
  endcomment
  assign border_width = 0
  if s.border_style == 'solid'
    assign border_width = s.border_width | default: 1 | plus: 0

    assign border_percent = s.border_opacity | default: 100 | plus: 0
    if s.border_color == blank
      assign border_paint = 'color-mix(in srgb, currentColor ' | append: border_percent | append: '%, transparent)'
    else
      assign border_alpha = border_percent | divided_by: 100.0
      assign border_paint = s.border_color | color_modify: 'alpha', border_alpha
    endif
  endif

  assign radius = s.border_radius | default: 0 | plus: 0
  assign margin_top = s.margin_top | default: 0 | plus: 0
  assign margin_bottom = s.margin_bottom | default: 0 | plus: 0

  comment
    ---- layout ----

    The arrangement used to be fixed: one column, heading cluster over the
    questions. It is now the merchant's, and the controls are the Group block's
    vocabulary rather than a second one invented here — Alignment is always the
    horizontal axis, Position always the vertical, and `base.css` decides which
    CSS property reads which based on the direction. `snippets/group.liquid`
    explains why that swap lives in one place.

    What this file does not do is guess which child is which. Horizontal is a
    flex row of the section's own children, so the heading cluster and the
    accordion sit side by side because they are siblings, not because a
    selector went looking for them.
  endcomment
  assign direction = s.direction | default: 'column'
  assign is_row = false
  if direction == 'row'
    assign is_row = true
  endif

  comment
    Two settings, one control. The horizontal list carries the distribution
    options on top of the three alignments, because on a row they land on the
    same `justify-content` and only one of the two could win. On a column they
    would be inert, so that list is the plain three and the merchant never sees
    an option that does nothing.
  endcomment
  if is_row
    assign alignment_setting = s.alignment_row | default: 'start'
  else
    assign alignment_setting = s.alignment | default: 'start'
  endif

  case alignment_setting
    when 'center'
      assign alignment_axis = 'center'
    when 'end'
      assign alignment_axis = 'end'
    else
      assign alignment_axis = 'start'
  endcase

  comment
    The alignment with the distribution folded in, and the plain one beside it.
    They differ exactly when a distribution is chosen, and the phone stack needs
    the plain one: `space-between` is valid on the `justify-content` it feeds on
    a desktop row and invalid on the `align-items` it would feed once stacked.
  endcomment
  assign inline_axis = alignment_axis
  if is_row
    case alignment_setting
      when 'space-between', 'space-around', 'space-evenly'
        assign inline_axis = alignment_setting
    endcase
  endif

  case s.position
    when 'center'
      assign block_axis = 'center'
    when 'end'
      assign block_axis = 'end'
    else
      assign block_axis = 'start'
  endcase

  comment
    `plus: 0` coerces the range to a number rather than relying on `default`
    alone, which would replace a deliberate 0 — a gap a merchant can legitimately
    want. Each mobile axis falls back to its desktop value, so a section that
    never opens Mobile layout behaves as it did.
  endcomment
  assign gap_x = s.gap_horizontal | default: 24 | plus: 0
  assign gap_y = s.gap_vertical | default: 24 | plus: 0
  assign gap_x_mobile = s.gap_horizontal_mobile | default: gap_x | plus: 0
  assign gap_y_mobile = s.gap_vertical_mobile | default: gap_y | plus: 0

  assign content_classes = 'faq__content faq__content--' | append: direction
  if is_row and s.stack_on_mobile
    assign content_classes = content_classes | append: ' faq__content--stack-mobile'
  endif
-%}

{%- capture content_style -%}
  --faq-content-gap-x: {{ gap_x }}px;
  --faq-content-gap-y: {{ gap_y }}px;
  --faq-content-gap-x-mobile: {{ gap_x_mobile }}px;
  --faq-content-gap-y-mobile: {{ gap_y_mobile }}px;
  --faq-content-inline: {{ inline_axis }};
  --faq-content-align: {{ alignment_axis }};
  --faq-content-block: {{ block_axis }};
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- capture section_style -%}
  {%- render 'spacing', section: s, declarations: true -%}
  --faq-radius: {{ radius }}px;
  --faq-margin-block-start: {{ margin_top }}px;
  --faq-margin-block-end: {{ margin_bottom }}px;
  {%- if border_width > 0 -%}
    --faq-border-width: {{ border_width }}px;
    --faq-border-color: {{ border_paint }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if background_paint != '' -%}
    background: {{ background_paint }};
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

<div
  class="faq color-scheme-container color-{{ s.color_scheme }}{% if has_background_media %} has-background-media{% endif %}"
  data-section-spacing
  style="{{ section_style | strip_newlines | strip }}"
>
  {%- if has_background_media -%}
    {% render 'background-media', settings: s %}
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="{% render 'container', width: s.container_width %}">
    {%- comment -%}
      `children: true` staggers the direct children — the heading cluster, then
      each accordion — so the section arrives as one cascade rather than as a
      block of text that appears all at once. The stagger is a setting; at its
      default of 0 they simply arrive together.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <motion-effect
      class="{{ content_classes }}"
      data-easing="outQuint"
      style="{{ content_style | strip_newlines | strip }}"
      {% render 'motion-attrs', kind: 'text', section: s, children: true %}
    >
      {% content_for 'block', type: 'section-header', id: 'faq-header' %}
      {% content_for 'blocks' %}
    </motion-effect>
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:sections.faq.name",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "@theme"
    },
    {
      "type": "@app"
    }
  ],
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "container_width",
      "label": "t:shared.container.width.label",
      "info": "t:shared.container.width.info",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "edge",
          "label": "t:shared.container.width.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "wide",
          "label": "t:shared.container.width.options__2.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "standard",
          "label": "t:shared.container.width.options__3.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "compact",
          "label": "t:shared.container.width.options__4.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "custom",
          "label": "t:shared.container.width.options__5.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "standard"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:blocks.group.headers.layout"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "direction",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.direction.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "column",
          "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.direction.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "row",
          "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.direction.options__2.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "column"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "stack_on_mobile",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.stack_on_mobile.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.group.settings.stack_on_mobile.info",
      "default": true,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.direction == 'row' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "alignment",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "start",
          "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "center",
          "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.options__2.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "end",
          "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.options__3.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "start",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.direction == 'column' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "alignment_row",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "start",
          "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "center",
          "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.options__2.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "end",
          "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.options__3.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "space-between",
          "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.distribution.options__2.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "space-around",
          "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.distribution.options__3.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "space-evenly",
          "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.distribution.options__4.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "start",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.direction == 'row' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "position",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.position.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "start",
          "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.position.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "center",
          "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.position.options__2.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "end",
          "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.position.options__3.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "start",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.direction == 'row' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "gap_horizontal",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.gap_horizontal.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 24
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "gap_vertical",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.gap_vertical.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 24
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:blocks.group.headers.mobile_layout"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "gap_horizontal_mobile",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.gap_horizontal.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 24
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "gap_vertical_mobile",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.gap_vertical.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 24
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:shared.appearance.header"
    },
    {
      "type": "color_scheme",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "t:shared.color_scheme.label",
      "default": "scheme-1"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "background_media",
      "label": "t:shared.background.media.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "none",
          "label": "t:shared.background.media.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "image",
          "label": "t:shared.background.media.options__2.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "none"
    },
    {
      "type": "color_background",
      "id": "background_color",
      "label": "t:shared.background.color.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.color.info",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media == 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "image",
      "label": "t:shared.background.image.label",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media == 'image' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "image_mobile",
      "label": "t:shared.background.image_mobile.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.image_mobile.info",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media == 'image' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "image_position",
      "label": "t:shared.background.image_position.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.image_position.info",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "cover",
          "label": "t:shared.background.image_position.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "fit",
          "label": "t:shared.background.image_position.options__2.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "cover",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media == 'image' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:blocks.group.headers.borders"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "border_style",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.border_style.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "none",
          "label": "t:shared.options.none"
        },
        {
          "value": "solid",
          "label": "t:shared.options.solid"
        }
      ],
      "default": "none"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "border_width",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.border_width.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 12,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 1,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.border_style == 'solid' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "border_opacity",
      "label": "t:shared.border.opacity.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 100,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.border_style == 'solid' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "border_color",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.border_color.label",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.border_style == 'solid' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "border_radius",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.border_radius.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 60,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:shared.animation.header"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "animation_text",
      "label": "t:shared.animation.animation_text.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "inherit",
          "label": "t:shared.animation.animation_text.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "none",
          "label": "t:shared.animation.animation_text.options__2.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "fade-in",
          "label": "t:shared.animation.animation_text.options__3.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "fade-up",
          "label": "t:shared.animation.animation_text.options__4.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "slide-up",
          "label": "t:shared.animation.animation_text.options__5.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "inherit"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "animation_duration",
      "label": "t:shared.animation.animation_duration.label",
      "info": "t:shared.animation.animation_duration.info",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 2000,
      "step": 100,
      "unit": "ms",
      "default": 1000
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "animation_stagger",
      "label": "t:shared.animation.animation_stagger.label",
      "info": "t:shared.animation.animation_stagger.info",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 300,
      "step": 10,
      "unit": "ms",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:shared.spacing.section_header"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "t:shared.spacing.section_paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
